  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Established in 1887, Clark University is located in the heart of Worcester, Massachusetts. As a research university, it provides opportunities to engage in research across a wide range of fields, from psychology and environmental science to economics.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>The University has a vibrant student community, with over 130 student clubs. You can participate in various clubs, such as the Clark Sustainability Collaborative and the International Students Association, among many others.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Clark University offers a variety of on-campus housing options.</p><p>You can choose from 3 co-ed residence halls that specifically cater to first-year students, or from 2 mixed-class halls. Further, there are 6 co-ed houses, including one designated as an Affinity House and another for graduate students.</p><p>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\">download our app</a> and check out the Stays feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The Goddard Library is the central hub for research, with an extensive collection of books, journals, and digital resources. The library offers quiet study areas and computer stations as well.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>Clark’s sports facilities include a fitness centre, outdoor athletic fields, and an indoor gymnasium. The University has a strong athletic program with a range of varsity, club, and intramural sports. The University is also a member of the NCAA Division III and offers sports such as basketball, soccer, and swimming.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>Clark provides state-of-the-art labs for environmental science, biology, and chemistry. Key facilities include the Lasry Center for Bioscience, Arthur M. Sackler Sciences Center, and other dedicated labs for psychology and physics.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>Clark University offers you diverse dining options and meal plans. The Table at Higgins at the Higgins University Centre is the common eating facility. Focuses on locally sourced sandwiches, paninis, salads, and a rotating menu of global cuisines. Similarly, the Bistro is another place to eat at the campus. Meanwhile, the Cougar Cafe provides you with quick snacks and beverages.</p><p>Beyond campus dining, Clark University is located near several restaurants and eateries, so you never stay hungry.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
